                        "entry_id": "a365f67f-cc54-3c97-b911-cc3c49b39ada",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A metal bulb filled with nitrous oxide gas, inhaled for its disassociative effects, normally intended as a propellant for whipped cream."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Australia",
                            "New-Zealand",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "14e1dbdd-a721-45af-a1fa-7791e101d8d5",
                                "sense_id": "978ad8e5-c1b3-3540-956d-a902340805f5",
                                "text": "I reckon the thing that brings on a trip the quickest is definitly^([sic]) a nang (nitrous oxide bulb) while listening to REALLY intense music"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "449e3c52-3328-4f1d-8331-2a902c20974e",
                                "sense_id": "978ad8e5-c1b3-3540-956d-a902340805f5",
                                "text": "\"helicopters\" these days refers to those silly hats with propellers on top, which come with a free ounce of smack at any local K-mart.^([sic]) Y'know, next to the nangs (or bulbs - nitrous oxide for whipped cream)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
